{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"textures versus materials in blender textures versus materials in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","fileName":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"textures versus materials in blender textures versus materials in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","fileName":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender","heading":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A texture provides patterned or image-derived data, while a material gathers the surface information applied to an object. One real-world surface may need coordinated color, diffuse, normal, alpha, and other maps that were designed as a set.\n\nBlender's material acts as the container for those related texture influences. A script creates and configures the constituent textures, associates them with the material, and assigns the material to the object. UV coordinates then determine how the material's image-based information is arranged over the mesh surface.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"textures versus materials in blender textures versus materials in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","fileName":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Textures Versus Materials in Blender","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}